'''Cala Tranquilla''' ({{lang|ca|Cala Tranquilla}}; Volisanian for "quiet cove") is a [[comarca]] on the [[Shendan Ocean]] coast of [[Tramuntana Province]], [[Balboa]]. It is the most populous and most densely populated comarca in the province, containing the provincial capital, [[Portblanc]], which accounts for the overwhelming majority of the comarca's population. The comarca had a population of 840,000 in 2026 and a density of 653.2/km², making it the demographic and economic centre of Tramuntana Province.

== Etymology ==

The name ''Cala Tranquilla'' (Volisanian for "quiet cove" or "tranquil bay") refers to the sheltered harbour at the mouth of which the city of [[Portblanc]] was established. The name was applied to the surrounding administrative district during the Volisanian colonial period and has been retained as the comarca designation in the modern provincial subdivision system.

== Geography ==

Cala Tranquilla is situated on the western coast of the Balboa isthmus, along the [[Shendan Ocean]]. The comarca extends from the coastline inland to the hills of the coastal Tramuntana range, a small elevated ridge that runs parallel to the Shendan coast, separate from and west of the main [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] highlands. The coastal plain is narrow, and the terrain rises steadily from the shore into the hillsides that characterise the interior portions of the comarca. The comarca has an area of 1,286 km².

The comarca is bounded by the [[La Cruïlla (comarca)|La Cruïlla]] comarca to the east and the [[El Mas (comarca)|El Mas]] comarca to the south. The [[Cala Negra (comarca)|Cala Negra]] comarca, an island territory offshore, lies to the west across the Shendan Ocean. The western boundary of the comarca is the Shendan Ocean coastline, which extends for approximately 27 kilometres.

=== Climate ===

The comarca has a {{w|tropical savanna climate}} that is unusually dry for the Shendan coastal region. A pronounced wet season lasts from May to November, with a dry season from December to April, but annual rainfall averages only approximately 800–1,000 mm — significantly lower than other coastal areas of the isthmus. The dryness is a consequence of the double rain shadow produced by the coastal Tramuntana range, which intercepts moisture-bearing winds from the Shendan Ocean, and the main [[Yalabirga Mountain Range|Yalabirga]] highlands to the east, which block humid air masses from the interior. The drying trend associated with {{w|climate change}} has increased the risk of {{w|grass fire|grass fires}} in the hills of the coastal Tramuntana range, particularly during the extended dry season.

== Settlements ==

The comarca's population is overwhelmingly concentrated in the city of [[Portblanc]], the provincial capital, which had an estimated population of 680,000 in 2026. The remaining population is distributed across smaller coastal settlements, agricultural communities on the inland periphery, and institutional installations.

